// Cloudflare Workers with Static Assets. There is no Worker script: the site is entirely
// static, so this file is the whole deployment.
//
//   npm run build            (VITE_BASE_PATH unset — vite.config.ts already defaults to "/")
//   npx wrangler deploy      (first time: `npx wrangler login`)
//
// Or connect the GitHub repository in the Cloudflare dashboard with build command
// `npm run build` and output directory `dist`, and it deploys on every push.
//
// The 3D app routes on the URL hash, so any path the host does not know is a real mistake.
// That is why this is "404-page" and not "single-page-application": the SPA setting would
// answer every crawler typo with a 200 and the 433 KB app, where this answers with
// public/404.html and a 404, which is what it should be. The default html_handling
// ("auto-trailing-slash") already sends /admin to /admin/ and /lite to /lite/.
//
// Custom domains here need the domain's nameservers on Cloudflare (free). If they cannot be
// moved, GitHub Pages takes a custom domain from any DNS host and is the better fit.
{
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "astroportfolio",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-11",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./dist/",
    "not_found_handling": "404-page"
  }
}
